I propose a new type of monster: no, not a lack critter, but something
with a similar effect: a master quantum mechanic.

While an ordinary quantum mechanic just teleports *you* around the
current level of the dungeon (and is thus a mere annoyance at worst) a
master quantum mechanic would, with each successful hit, teleport one
of your *possessions* away.

The master quantum mechanic hits! -more-
The +7 Tsurugi (wielded) suddenly vanishes!
The master quantum mechanic hits! -more-
Your wand of death (1:3) suddenly vanishes!
The master quantum mechanic hits! -more-
Your blessed greased bag named "holding" suddenly vanishes!

The said item would have a fairly high chance of ending of somewhere
on the current level of the dungeon. However, it could also be
transported to a *different* dungeon level either above or below your
current position, with a decreasing (but non-zero) chance of
teleporting to level X the further away X is, to mimic true quantum-
mechanical behavior.

Thus, you'd have to slog through the dungeon, looking for said item,
which is quite likely going to end up in the hands of some hostile
monster before you get it back. *Which* hostile monster has it is
another problem for you to figure out. The Tsurugi/Vorpal Blade would
be particularly deadly in this scenario, but even a wand of death
could be a YASD unless you're magic resistant.

A good way to throw another interesting obstacle into the boring late
game.

Artemis the Ranger



